# Aegis Cognitive Defense Platform: Comprehensive Features & Functions Report

This document outlines every major technical domain, feature, and corresponding core function utilized within the Aegis Cognitive Defense Platform. 

## 1. Digital Signal Processing (DSP) & Radar Engineering
*Domain: Physics, Data Science, and Mathematics*

**Core Features & Capabilities:**
*   **Synthetic Signal Generation:** Creates highly realistic radar echo wave data based on the laws of physics, complete with simulated noise, clutter, and Doppler shifts.
*   **Fast Fourier Transforms (FFT):** Converts raw time-domain signal data into frequency models to extract target velocity (Doppler) and distance (Range).
*   **Target Detection CFAR:** Employs advanced algorithms to filter out background noise and identify valid radar spikes as targets.

**Key Functions Used:**
*   [matched_filter(received, template)](file:///c:/Users/nikhil/Desktop/MCA%20Project/Aegis-Cognitive-Defense-Platform/src/detection.py#15-24): Maximizes Signal-to-Noise Ratio (SNR) by applying FFT convolution to compare the received signal against the transmitted template.
*   [range_doppler_map(pulses, n_range, n_doppler)](file:///c:/Users/nikhil/Desktop/MCA%20Project/Aegis-Cognitive-Defense-Platform/src/detection.py#26-33): Applies a 2D Fast Fourier Transform (`np.fft.fft2`) to map raw radar pulses into 2D matrices showing Range and Doppler space.
*   [ca_cfar(rd_map, guard, train, pfa)](file:///c:/Users/nikhil/Desktop/MCA%20Project/Aegis-Cognitive-Defense-Platform/src/detection.py#35-78): Executes Cell-Averaging Constant False Alarm Rate (CA-CFAR) detection. Averages background noise cells to dynamically set detection thresholds using 2D image convolution.
*   [os_cfar(rd_map, guard, train, rank, pfa)](file:///c:/Users/nikhil/Desktop/MCA%20Project/Aegis-Cognitive-Defense-Platform/src/detection.py#80-119): Executes Order-Statistic CFAR. Sorts background noise cells arrays and selects a specific rank to establish detection thresholds (optimal for multiple close targets).
*   [detect_targets_from_raw(signal, fs, n_range, n_doppler)](file:///c:/Users/nikhil/Desktop/MCA%20Project/Aegis-Cognitive-Defense-Platform/src/detection.py#121-157): The master DSP pipeline function that chains FFT transformation with CFAR detection to return exact [(X, Y)](file:///c:/Users/nikhil/Desktop/MCA%20Project/Aegis-Cognitive-Defense-Platform/api/routes/auth.py#26-33) coordinate matrices of valid targets.

